],"startLine":163,"endLine":168,"firstParagraph":"Signing verification consumes the complete identity list before deciding success, so early pipe closure cannot reject a valid Developer ID identity under `pipefail`.","githubSlug":"identity-output-consumption"}],"startLine":157,"endLine":162,"firstParagraph":"Stable and beta release jobs import the Developer ID certificate into a workflow-owned temporary keychain before packaging, making signing reliable across GitHub runner updates.","githubSlug":"macos-signing-keychain"},{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates#Stable and beta release channels#Native module packaging","heading":"Native module packaging","depth":3,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[],"startLine":169,"endLine":174,"firstParagraph":"Stable and beta macOS builds verify the exact architecture-specific `better-sqlite3` prebuild that the packaged runtime loads.","githubSlug":"native-module-packaging"},{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates#Stable and beta release channels#Production package contents","heading":"Production package contents","depth":3,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[],"startLine":175,"endLine":182,"firstParagraph":"The application archive contains compiled outputs, runtime resources, package metadata, the project license and production dependencies; repository development material is excluded.","githubSlug":"production-package-contents"},{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates#Stable and beta release channels#Platform package identity","heading":"Platform package identity","depth":3,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[],"startLine":183,"endLine":188,"firstParagraph":"Linux packages use the space-free `/opt/HermesOne` directory while macOS keeps the existing `Hermes One.app` bundle and executable name. RPM filenames retain the `.rpm` extension expected by release uploads.","githubSlug":"platform-package-identity"},{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates#Stable and beta release channels#Linux package sandbox and AppArmor","heading":"Linux package sandbox and AppArmor","depth":3,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates#Stable and beta release channels#Linux package sandbox and AppArmor#Compatible profile installation","heading":"Compatible profile installation","depth":4,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[],"startLine":199,"endLine":202,"firstParagraph":"Both actual generated package hooks copy the exact bundled profile bytes and load the installed policy after parser compatibility succeeds.","githubSlug":"compatible-profile-installation"},{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates#Stable and beta release channels#Linux package sandbox and AppArmor#Unsupported AppArmor","heading":"Unsupported AppArmor","depth":4,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[],"startLine":203,"endLine":206,"firstParagraph":"Disabled AppArmor and an incompatible parser skip policy copying and kernel loading without turning a platform compatibility skip into a package failure.","githubSlug":"unsupported-apparmor"},{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates#Stable and beta release channels#Linux package sandbox and AppArmor#Image-building chroot","heading":"Image-building chroot","depth":4,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[],"startLine":207,"endLine":210,"firstParagraph":"A compatible profile is copied into an image-building chroot while kernel loading is skipped, preserving the host's policy state.","githubSlug":"image-building-chroot"},{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates#Stable and beta release channels#Linux package sandbox and AppArmor#Real load failures remain visible","heading":"Real load failures remain visible","depth":4,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[],"startLine":211,"endLine":214,"firstParagraph":"A compatible policy that fails actual kernel loading retains its nonzero result, rather than being silently treated as an unsupported parser.","githubSlug":"real-load-failures-remain-visible"},{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates#Stable and beta release channels#Linux package sandbox and AppArmor#Conditional sandbox permission","heading":"Conditional sandbox permission","depth":4,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[],"startLine":215,"endLine":217,"firstParagraph":"Working user namespaces preserve sandbox mode 0755, while unavailable namespaces select the SUID mode needed by Chromium's alternate sandbox path.","githubSlug":"conditional-sandbox-permission"}],"startLine":189,"endLine":198,"firstParagraph":"DEB and RPM packages use Electron Builder's complete default post-install hook so compatible AppArmor policy is installed alongside sandbox permissions and desktop integration.","githubSlug":"linux-package-sandbox-and-apparmor"}],"startLine":121,"endLine":130,"firstParagraph":"Two GitHub Actions workflows publish builds; only the stable channel reaches end users' auto-update, so a beta can be tested without risking their devices.","githubSlug":"stable-and-beta-release-channels"}],"startLine":1,"endLine":10,"firstParagraph":"Desktop updates use GitHub releases and expose both a startup upgrade action and a Settings auto-upgrade preference.","githubSlug":"desktop-updates"}],"headingTitles":["Desktop Updates","Desktop installation channel","Progress evidence","Measured download events","Unknown totals do not imply completion","Invalid percent remains unknown","About download measurements","Unknown and inactive download feedback","Agent phases","About phase lifetime","Changed profile rejects old progress","Changed connection rejects old progress","Unmount releases the progress lis